insane hospital", "an insane asylum"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Causing insanity or madness.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Were such things here, as we doe speake about? / Or haue we eaten on the insane Root, / That takes the Reason Prisoner?", "reference": "c. 1606 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Tragedie of Macbeth”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act I, scene iii]:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "подлудя́ващ"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "storend"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "dérangeant"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "démentiel"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "malsain"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "enlouquecedor"}, {"language": {"code": "ro", "name": "Romanian"}, "word": "demențial"}, {"language": {"code": "ro", "name": "Romanian"}, "word": "înnebunitor"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal) Characterized by excess or the utmost folly; ridiculous; impractical.", "tags": ["informal"], "examples": ["an insane plan", "an insane amount of money"], "quotes": [{"text": "The preposterous altruism too![…]Resist not evil. It is an insane immolation of self—as bad intrinsically as fakirs stabbing themselves or anchorites warping their spines in caves scarcely large enough for a fair-sized dog.", "reference": "1918, W[illiam] B[abington] Maxwell, chapter XVI, in The Mirror and the Lamp, Indianapolis, Ind.: The Bobbs-Merrill Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Yenshui is a fairly ordinary town situated between Tainan and Chiayi. However, during the Lantern Festival, on the 15th day of the first moon, the whole town goes insane.", "r